DTEND:20260816T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260803T084935Z
UID:3ebe5225-8af7-5e70-b460-6c6bfcbc33c1
DESCRIPTION:(https://www.cycleto.ca/rec_hub)\n\nThe Cycle Toronto Rec Hub 
 at Evergreen Brick Works is a welcoming community space that takes the int
 imidation out of bike maintenance and repair.\n\nIF YOU'RE A TRAINED CYCLE
  TORONTO REC HUB VOLUNTEER\, SIGN UP FOR SUPPORT SHIFTS.\n\nOur friendly s
 taff and volunteers will help guide you through the basics to keep you rol
 ling. Even expert home mechanics are also welcome to use our facilities.\n
 \nDIY service is first come\, first serve.\n\nFind out more: (https://www.
 cycleto.ca/rec_hub) cycleto.ca/rec_hub\nURL: https://www.cycleto.ca/rec_hu
 b_diy_20260816
LOCATION:Rec Hub at Evergreen Brick Works\n550 Bayview Avenue\nToronto ON 
 M4W 3X8\nCA
URL:https://www.cycleto.ca/rec_hub_diy_20260816
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coffee Outside Group Ride
DTSTART:20260816T120000Z
DTEND:20260816T120000Z
DTSTAMP:20260803T084934Z
UID:41aaaca6-f17a-5239-ba5a-87b151e82a0f
DESCRIPTION:Join us for Coffee Outside\, a leisurely group ride along the 
 Don River trail system. We'll roll at a chill pace\, take in the greenery\
 , and stop for coffee and conversation at a scenic spot along the way. All
  bikes and all speeds are welcome. Just bring your mug\, your favourite br
 ew fixings\, and enjoy the morning.\n\nDoors: 8 AM\n\nSession: 8:00-10 AM\
 n\nLight snacks provided\nURL: https://www.cycleto.ca/coffee_outside_group
 _ride
LOCATION:Evergreen Brickworks\n550 Bayview Ave\n10\nToronto ON M4W 3X8\nCA
URL:https://www.cycleto.ca/coffee_outside_group_ride
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ride The Track 2026
DTSTART:20260814T210000Z
DTEND:20260815T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20260803T084935Z
UID:45d2330b-583c-523c-beb2-990318df30d9
DESCRIPTION:Ride the Track 2026 on the Markham Indy Track!\n\nExperience t
 he thrill of riding the Honda Indy track on your own bicycle while support
 ing a great cause!\n\nRide the Track returns on Friday\, August 14\, 2026\
 , at the Markham Pan Am Centre\, giving cyclists\, families\, and communit
 y members the unique opportunity to ride the closed course in support of T
 he Children's Breakfast Clubs.\n\nWhether you're a seasoned cyclist or sim
 ply looking for a fun family activity\, everyone is welcome to join us for
  an unforgettable evening of cycling and community spirit.\n\nEvent Detail
 s\n\nDate: Friday\, August 14\, 2026\nTime: Registration opens at 5:00 PM 
 | Ride begins at 6:30 PM\nLocation: Markham Pan Am Centre\, Markham\, ON\n
 Registration: $25 per rider\n\nNote: Children under 6 ride free when ridin
 g on an adult's bicycle with a parent or guardian. Children aged 6 and old
 er may ride independently.\n\nEvery registration helps support The Childre
 n's Breakfast Clubs\, providing hot\, nutritious meals to children in more
  than 40 communities across Southern Ontario. With $0.87 of every dollar r
 aised going directly toward programs and services\, your ride makes a real
  difference.\n\nGather your friends\, bring the family\, and enjoy this on
 e-of-a-kind opportunity to ride the track while helping children start the
 ir day with a healthy breakfast.\n\nLearn more and register: (https://brea
 kfastclubs.ca/) https://breakfastclubs.ca/\nURL: https://www.cycleto.ca/14
 9988/ride_the_track_2026
LOCATION:Markham Pan Am Centre\n16 Main St Unionville\nMarkham ON L3R 0W7\
 nCA
URL:https://www.cycleto.ca/149988/ride_the_track_2026
END:VEVENT
